speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, pursuant to Standing Order 43, I request unanimous consent of the House to move a motion on a pressing matter of extreme importance.
As the choices to be made, as a result of the budget speech of June 23 last, will be essentially of a political nature;
As the Minister of Finance is incapable, with the present policy, to fight inflation;
As the increase in the price of natural gas and heating oil, as announced by the Minister of Finance in his budget speech, will constitute too heavy a burden for the average-income taxpayers, I move, seconded by the hon. member for Bellechasse (Mr. Lambert):
That a compensated discount be applied to heating oil and natural gas, with a view to enabling Canadians, whose income is less than $12,000 a year, to heat their homes in spite of the increase in prices.
